# Template for /etc/stillwell.env (0600, root-owned), read by stillwell-ingest.service, stillwell-jobs.service
# and every job it starts. apply.sh installs it on a box that has no file yet and never overwrites an existing one.

# The public store, which the poller reads over HTTPS (docs/plans/realtime.md).
STILLWELL_STORE=https://stillwell.openwaters.io
# The store the job queue's jobs write, as their STILLWELL_STORE, with an R2 token that may read and write the
# water-levels bucket, as the `lake` environment's secrets. Store jobs wait until these are set (docs/plans/jobs.md).
STILLWELL_WRITE_STORE=s3://water-levels
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# The restricted store, needed only once an hourly source bars republishing; the poller refuses to start
# without it then.
# STILLWELL_RESTRICTED_STORE=
# ClickHouse on loopback, as config.d/stillwell.xml has it. apply.sh adds CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD, generated on
# the box, and sets it on ClickHouse's default user; the client reads it from here.
CLICKHOUSE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8123
# The api.data.gov key, the same one Actions uses; USGS requests pace themselves to leave the poller room in its
# hourly budget (pacing in src/sources/usgs/index.ts).
USGS_API_KEY=
# A key from the Channel Coastal Observatory, and the domain it was issued for, which the adapter sends as its Referer.
# The poller never asks CCO (its metadata sets `poller: "recent"`); store jobs for it on the job queue need them.
CCO_API_KEY=
CCO_REFERER=
# A fine-grained token for openwatersio/stillwell with Actions: read and write, so a source that reports a
# station in another datum starts its Monthly refresh. Without it the server logs the change and goes on.
# stillwell-jobs reads it too, to see that no Actions run still writes a source before it does, and starts
# no store job without it.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# stillwell-ingest.service sets STILLWELL_METRICS and STILLWELL_FROM_RECENT itself. A line here for either
# replaces the unit's value rather than adding to it.
